<title>SOUTH AFRICA: South Africa forecasts bigger 1996/97 wheat crop.</title>
<headline>South Africa forecasts bigger 1996/97 wheat crop.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African wheat production is expected to rise to 2.534 million tonnes in 1996/97 from a revised 1.969 million tonnes in 1995/96, the National Crop Estimates Committee said in its first forecast.  </p>
<p>The bigger crop is expected despite a decline in the area sown to 1.27 million hectares from 1.36 million last season.</p>
<p>Analysts attribute the healthier crop to plentiful water supplies following soaking summer rains.</p>
<p>The new crop will be harvested from November. The bulk of the crop is produced in the Western Cape and Free State provinces.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
